    {
      "name": "UsbConfigDxe",
      "guid": "cd823a4d-7dec-4531-ae5d-4134fa4127b8",
      "pe_sha256": "4d1672431e7f7e0a74670008ba31809fa3364667754470589e29dcfba66a1675",
      "depex_sha256": "ee32169774c787d62e03f2d39f9f266977871fec5c433e46b4c03e29b8abd17e",
      "binary_patch": {
        "module": "UsbConfigDxe",
        "input_sha256": "c56a7783d544d0b1446c5add31c94dd8d8baa9db75b8201b57fb45dc04a3c253",
        "output_sha256": "4d1672431e7f7e0a74670008ba31809fa3364667754470589e29dcfba66a1675",
        "sites": [
          {
            "rva": "0x143f0",
            "before": "0000000003000000",
            "after": "0000000001000000",
            "meaning": "Select host mode (1) only for physical USB core 0. Leave the absent second core disabled (0), as in TB520FU stock; the live DT has one DWC3 controller at 0x0a600000.",
            "evidence": "Our mode array is `03 00 00 00` immediately before the ASCII \"usbc\" struct base at 0x143F8 (stride 0x130), the same placement as bitra/9707f (`03 03` before \"usbc\" at 0x15360). bitra UsbConfigDxe.hostmode.efi and 9707f UsbConfigDxe.patched.efi change exactly those bytes 03 -> 01, and our whole mode-switch block 0x4480-0x4680 is byte-identical to giulia's stock build.",
            "reference": "https://github.com/Project-Silicium/Device-Binaries/blob/main/bitra/QcomPkg/Drivers/UsbConfigDxe/UsbConfigDxe.hostmode.efi"
          },
          {
            "rva": "0x47a4",
            "before": "a0035e38e1031f2a00013fd6a0831ff8",
            "after": "a0035e382100805200013fd6a0831ff8",
            "meaning": "Pass mode argument 1 instead of 0 to the USB core start entry (`mov w1,wzr ; blr x8` becomes `mov w1,#1 ; blr x8`) on the host start path the mode byte selects.",
            "evidence": "Same edit exists in bitra UsbConfigDxe.hostmode.efi (both copies of the call, at 0x4638 and 0x472C); our build has this one copy at 0x47A8. The driver's own fallback start path at 0x47D8 already passes w1 = 1 to the local UsbStartController, so 1 is the value this code treats as \"start\".",
            "reference": "https://github.com/Project-Silicium/Device-Binaries/blob/main/bitra/QcomPkg/Drivers/UsbConfigDxe/UsbConfigDxe.hostmode.efi"
          }
        ],
        "limitations": "Host selection alone does not establish USB enumeration or VBUS. PMIC transfers have been restored with ownership checks, but need tablet verification. No Y703 or bitra GPIO/power data is imported.",
        "boot_tested": false
      }
    },
